{
  "version": 1,
  "questionId": "q22",
  "speechText": "Recently, I have been working on a clinical trial management system for a US-based company. My main role is backend development. I work mainly with NestJS and PostgreSQL, and recently I also worked a lot with AI document processing. One important part was the OCR pipeline. When users upload a document, the system needs to process it, run OCR, and prepare the content for the next AI steps. We had a problem because OCR was running on the CPU worker. For large documents, it was very slow and sometimes caused memory problems. So first, I traced the whole processing flow and checked the logs, memory usage, and processing time. Then I improved the CPU flow with smaller batches, checkpoint, and recovery logic. After that, I worked with DevOps to move the OCR inference to a separate GPU service. This gave us a very good result. The processing time improved from around 46 seconds per page to around 2 seconds per page. Another part I am working on is an agent workflow system called StrangeLoop. The main idea is instead of only asking the LLM to answer directly, the workflow can use different tools to search or read data from our system. Then the backend still controls the important parts, such as validation, permission, and tool execution. For this part, I also work with DevOps to set up the infrastructure, service connection, environment, and authentication. So overall, this project gives me experience not only in normal backend development, but also in AI production systems, GPU inference, agent workflows, and system reliability.",
